WEBVTT

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:07.990
I am in love with you.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.980
<b>I am in love with you.</b>

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:13.870
What did you say?

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:15.610
\beginnnnnnoooooooowhaaaaaaawhatsgoingonnnnnnnnkuw

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.990
corresponds with emotions of love.
A number of concrete examples follow:
"When I feel my genes are telling me that we are compatible."
"When I hug them, all my tiredness flies away."
"Every gesture and movement is dear to me."
"I want to be near them. I want to hold them."
"When I'm having a hard time, I want them to comfort me."
"I want this love to be mutual."
"I want to be close enough to be able to respond to those emotions with everything I have"
etc. These concrete examples are consistent with the points of commonality in Love Group A as well as the selection of topics established in the experiments.

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:25.360
It was a little different 
from that other time.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.880
<b>I am in love with you.</b>

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.950
I seem to be in love with you.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.750
<b>I seem to be in love with you.</b>

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.590
<i>You remember it.</i>

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:35.070
Very well.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.330
Let me hear your proof of love.

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:41.760
What theory did you use to 
determine that you love me?

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:46.770
Indeed. To make a determination 
without some kind of theory...

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:50.010
would make me a failure as an 
Info-Sci student, wouldn't it?

