00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:16.760
So, what is all this?

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:19.400
We're only doing experiments 
like ones we've done before.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.350
It's time to tell me what your aims are.

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:26.230
We really have done all kinds 
of things, haven't we?

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.560
Measuring heart rates.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:29.970
Emotion counters.

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:31.080
Kiss experiments.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.270
Saliva analysis.

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.670
And so many others.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:36.370
Yes.

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:39.870
But there is no point to 
having our data alone.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.150
Yes.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:46.250
That's why we asked Yamamoto-senpai to help 
us gather love data from lots of people.

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:49.450
The "love" of many people.

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:54.240
There were so many emotions, 
such variety in forms of affection...

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.800
a flood of diverse stories.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.570
It didn't seem possible to find 
any points of commonality.

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:03.660
But I did discover one thing.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:08.500
Who was it that decided that 
each of them loved someone?

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:11.290
It was personal, 
unsubstantiated assertion, wasn't it?

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.290
<i>That's right!</i>

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:21.800
<b>Points of Commonality?</b>

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:21.800
<b>Love A</b>

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:18.900
<i>We have been assembling people 
who are in a state of love</i>

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:21.800
<b>Love B</b>

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:21.800
<b>Love C</b>

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:21.800
<b>Love D</b>

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:21.800
<b>Love E</b>

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:21.790
<i>and trying to find points 
of commonality from there.</i>

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:27.040
<i>But what are the criterion for determining 
that a person is in a state of love?</i>

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:33.060
<b>Yaaay</b>

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.640
I am in love with someone!

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:33.060
<i>That is either left to those 
individuals' personal assertions...</i>

