00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:36.560
<b>Contact
Ikeda Laboratory</b>

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:36.500
<i>or determined by meeting certain conditions.</i>

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:40.860
<b>Points of Commonality:</b>

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:40.860
Heart races when
they get close.

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:39.480
<i>But when people are gathered 
based on particular conditions,</i>

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:42.740
<i>that condition itself becomes 
a point of commonality.</i>

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:46.700
<i>And that also happens in the 
case of personal assertion!</i>

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:51.440
Ultimately, the conditions 
of love are not absolute.

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:54.130
Either the person decides 
it arbitrarily themselves,

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:57.920
or we arbitrarily decide 
on certain criterion.

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:01.710
But Chris-senpai said something...

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:04.650
No matter what anyone might say...

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:06.860
No matter what theories it 
means I must violate...

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:09.220
I love Sui!

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:10.840
<i>Which means...</i>

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:12.100
<b>When I see him, my heart jumps out of my chest.</b>

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:14.080
<i>with the multitude of 
"loves" we have seen...</i>

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:13.310
<b>When he's with someone of the opposite gender, I hate it!</b>

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:14.810
<b>When we're together, even if we don't say
anything, it doesn't feel oppressive.</b>

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:17.500
<i>if we were able to pick out at 
least one point of commonality...</i>

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:15.810
<b>When I went to his funeral, I cried as much as his family did.</b>

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:16.810
<b>She smiled and said, "My hands are warm, aren't they?"
and my heart skipped a beat.</b>

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:17.560
<b>When I hug him, all my fatigue flies away!</b>

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:17.730
<b>Just getting a text from him makes me grin.</b>

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:21.160
<i>then the definition of love 
we've been searching for...</i>

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:24.860
I had fun today, Yukimura-kun.

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:26.300
Thank you.

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:29.600
<i>Definition 1, 1.</i>

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:32.610
<i>The condition which determines 
that A loves B is...</i>

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:39.290
<b>Definition 1.1</b>

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:39.340
<i>"A is cognizant of their love for B."</i>

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:39.290
<b>The condition which determines that A loves B is</b>

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:39.290
<b>"A is cognizant of their love for B."</b>

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:57.560
<i>I gave Kanade advice, 
but I didn't realize it myself.</i>

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:03.310
<i>That's right. The only one who can 
decide how you feel is you, yourself.</i>

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:07.860
<i>The moment that a person realizes 
that they love someone...</i>

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.890
<i>is the moment it becomes "love."</i>

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:12.780
<i>Say, Yukimura-kun.</i>

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:16.430
<i>Why do you think we went out and 
did all kinds of experiments?</i>

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:21.690
<i>For me, the time I spent with 
you researching romance...</i>

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:23.860
<i>has truly been fun.</i>

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:25.170
<i>I was happy.</i>

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:29.370
<i>This might be the last time, 
so I wanted to do it again.</i>

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:33.130
<i>After all, once I say my conclusions aloud,</i>

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:35.210
<i>our research will end.</i>

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:38.320
<i>There will be no more need 
to conduct experiments.</i>

00:07:39.010 --> 00:07:41.180
<i>And after our research is done...</i>

00:07:41.740 --> 00:07:44.120
<i>What will happen to our relationship?</i>

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:47.550
<i>I wonder if something will 
inevitably end up changing.</i>

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:51.790
<i>Oh, it's all too much trouble.</i>

00:07:52.190 --> 00:07:54.270
<i>Can't I just pretend nothing happened?</i>

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:56.980
<i>We don't have to produce the 
results of our research.</i>

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:00.070
<i>We could just put off 
giving our conclusions...</i>

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:03.140
<i>I wish we could just keep 
researching forever.</i>

00:08:03.140 --> 00:08:06.220
<i>It doesn't matter if we're in love or not.</i>

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:08.850
<i>Just being with you, the way we have been,</i>

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:11.950
<i>asking, "Could it be this?" 
or "Could it be that?"</i>

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:18.460
<i>If I could just... keep researching 
with you forever...</i>

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:21.480
Himuro?

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:23.290
<i>No.</i>

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:25.590
<i>Momentary emotions</i>

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:28.640
<i>cannot be permitted to 
distort research results.</i>

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:31.820
<i>My pride will not allow it.</i>

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:33.970
<i>I would fail as a science-type.</i>

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:36.430
<i>I would have no right to stand beside you.</i>

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:40.640
<i>Make yourself presentable!</i>

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:44.740
Yukimura-kun, I had fun today.

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:48.010
I was happy to be able to do all 
those experiments with you.

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:49.930
<i>Look to the future!</i>

00:08:49.930 --> 00:08:54.430
Researching love with you made me happy.

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:59.520
<i>Be confident, beautiful, and dignified!</i>

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:03.210
Therefore, today, on those grounds...

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:06.090
I will make an arbitrary decision 
regarding my emotions.

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:13.310
I am in love with you.

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:19.030
Science Fell in Love,
So I Tried to Prove It [<b>r=1-sinθ</b>]

00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:27.050
<i>Strangely, the mood value 
in that place was high.</i>

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:30.590
<i>There was no one in the research 
tower so late at night.</i>

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:35.140
<i>The hush of night didn't 
even reach 20 decibels.</i>

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:38.360
<i>The lights were off in the hallway,</i>

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:42.230
<i>and the starlight streaming in from the 
asterisms above barely measured 30 lumens.</i>

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:46.140
<i>Even as surface tension held back 
that which threatened to spill over,</i>

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:49.600
<i>still she was confident, 
beautiful, and dignified.</i>

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:52.240
<i>As Himuro said she loved me...</i>

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:54.930
<i>it was entirely impossible to quantify...</i>

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:56.590
<i>how beautiful she was.</i>

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:59.630
<i>Definition 1, 1.</i>

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:02.240
<i>The condition which determines 
that A loves B is</i>

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:06.750
<i>"A is cognizant of their love for B."</i>

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:08.960
<i>Based on that hypothesis,</i>

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:12.260
<i>Himuro has concluded that she loves me.</i>

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:15.000
<i>Then what about me?</i>

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:17.420
<i>Since that day,</i>

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:20.050
<i>I haven't been able to understand 
what is worthy of the term "love."</i>

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:22.190
<i>And I've been searching 
desperately for that answer.</i>

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:24.900
<i>But the conclusion is...</i>

00:10:25.610 --> 00:10:29.100
<i>that it's all right to 
determine it arbitrarily!</i>

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:30.270
<i>But how?</i>

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:33.800
<i>How, without using a basis with 
some degree of certainty?</i>

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:36.160
<i>Do you just decide things 
based on supposition?</i>

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:40.240
<i>If dragging things out and fretting 
hasn't produced a conclusion,</i>

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:42.680
<i>then turning those feelings into an equation</i>

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:47.050
<i>and using those values to decide 
things would be more constructive!</i>

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:50.080
<i>Telling someone else to do it...</i>

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:52.780
<i>and being unable to do it 
myself is too undignified.</i>

00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:56.390
Yukimura-kun?

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:59.760
I cannot produce a conclusion 
the way you have.

00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:03.790
I am organizing my emotions and 
turning them into an equation

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:06.690
so that I can determine 
whether or not I love you.

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:10.910
Positive emotions toward Himuro 
receive positive values.

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:16.070
Her smile is great!

00:11:10.910 --> 00:11:14.290
Negative emotions are expressed 
through negative values.

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:16.070
Her grinding
her teeth is annoying.

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:16.350
If the combined value is greater than zero,

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:18.570
If greater than 0, then it is

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:18.570
<b>Love</b>

00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:18.580
then that will arbitrarily 
determine my love.

